# POST /call — a call DOWN, from the parent to the node's admin plane.
#
# The body is a curl configuration for ONE request, already signed with the
# parent's key (RFC 9421) for the address the node hears: 127.0.0.1 and its
# admin port. This rule only carries it: the exec runs `curl -K -` on the node
# with that configuration on stdin. The workspace has no inbound route, so the
# provider's exec is the path.
#
# Nothing on the workspace can make this request: the node holds the parent's
# PUBLIC key only. (GET /unsigned is the same request without a signature.)
#
# This is the spike's stand-in. The built form is a request verb, where the
# parent chassis signs what it sends and no rule touches a signature.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.method == "POST" && @web.req.url.path == "/call"
  EXEC "workspace://node/exec"
    WITH command = "curl -sS -m 30 -K -",
         timeout = "40s",
         into    = "_out",
         stdin   = &b64decode(@web.req.body)
